 in Week 12","description":"UCLA and Ohio State fell, and three teams joined the list. How did the top 25 change after a wild Week 12?","published":"2026-11-23T12:14:22.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50545207/2026-college-football-power-rankings-top-25-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Tennessee fined by SEC after fans throw golf balls on field","description":"Tennessee was fined $250,000 by the SEC after fans threw golf balls and mustard bottles onto the football field late during Saturday's win over LSU.","published":"2026-11-23T01:42:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50568028/tennessee-fined-sec-fans-throw-golf-balls-field","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Alex Scarborough","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Notre Dame loses safety Luke Talich to torn Achilles","description":"Notre Dame starting safety Luke Talich sustained a torn right Achilles tendon in Saturday's win against SMU, sources told ESPN.","published":"2026-11-22T23:15:45.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50566676/notre-dame-loses-safety-luke-talich-torn-achilles","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Pete Thamel and Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What Week 12's unexpected results mean for Rivalry Week and beyond","description":"After another chaotic weekend, we look at the playoff and conference races on the line with one game to go.","published":"2026-11-22T23:54:19.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50563018/week-12-results-rivalry-week","type":"Story","byline":"Bill Connelly","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2027 recruit AJ Randle Jr. flips from Miami to Notre Dame","description":"Notre Dame coach Marcus Freeman flipped Miami pledge AJ Randle Jr., ESPN's No. 9 outside linebacker in the 2027 recruiting class, to fill a late-cycle need.","published":"2026-11-22T22:48:18.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50565158/2027-recruit-aj-randle-jr-flips-miami-notre-dame","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Pac-12 reveals unique flex schedule for season's final week","description":"The Pac-12 announced its unique flex schedule for the final week of the regular season early Sunday morning.","published":"2026-11-22T21:20:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564960/pac-12-reveals-unique-flex-schedule-season-final-week","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Montana State ranked No. 1, 5-7 LIU makes FCS bracket as conference champ","description":"Defending national champion Montana State received the top seed for the 24-team FCS playoffs, while Northeast Conference champion LIU (5-7) became the first playoff team with a losing record since 2017.","published":"2026-11-23T00:02:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50564910/montana-state-grabs-top-seed-24-team-fcs-playoff-bracket","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5145410/chris-cole","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Cole_(linebacker)"},"pick":{"pick":9,"round":1,"team":"PHI","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Chris Cole (linebacker)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chris_Cole_(linebacker)","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-22T23:50:20Z","intro":"Christopher Cole (born October 3, 2005) is an American college football linebacker for the Georgia Bulldogs.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Cole attended Salem High School in Salem, Virginia. As a junior, he recorded 76 tackles and 11 tackles-for-loss. A four-star recruit and one of the top-rated players in the state of Virginia, Cole committed to play college football at the University of Georgia over offers from Miami, Penn State, and Tennessee."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a true freshman, Cole totaled 16 tackles and two fumble recoveries, being named to the SEC All-Freshman Team. Entering the 2025 season, he was expected to earn a bigger role in the Bulldogs defense. Cole finished the season recording 60 tackles and 4.5 sacks.Against Oklahoma in 2026, he recorded a sack and two fumble recoveries, returning one 85 yards for a touchdown in a 41–13 victory. Cole was named SEC Defensive Player of the Week for his performance. He was named a Butkus Award semifinalist in October."}]}}